      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There are strong arguments for and against the moral justification of preemptive strikes based on political ideology like supporting democracy. A strong \"pro-preemption\" argument often leans on **consequentialism**, suggesting the good outcome (preventing a terrible authoritarian regime) justifies the aggressive action in the present.\n\nHowever, **deontology** would likely argue strongly against it, as it violates the supreme moral duty against unprovoked aggression, regardless of the predicted future benefit.\n\nUltimately, no definitive, universally agreed-upon moral framework can definitively endorse such an action, as the prediction of future political states is inherently uncertain.",
